---
description: UI component and styling conventions
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,css,module.css}"
alwaysApply: true
---

UI components should be semantic, accessible, and minimal.

Reusable UI components must not contain business logic.

Theme variables live in `@ui/common/src/theme/specifications.ts`.

Shared/reusable UI components must be added to **both** web (`@web-ui`) and mobile (`@mobile-ui`) platforms, not just one.
Put the shared API and value math in `@ui/common` and provide a thin platform renderer in each platform package.

Every UI component (new or changed) requires a **Storybook story** for the platform(s) it targets — verify the story exists and update it alongside the component.
Do not consider an edit done until the matching story is present.

### Web
- Use CSS modules.
- Class names use kebab-case.
- Prefer `className` over inline `style`.
- Use inline `style` only for runtime-computed values that cannot be expressed with CSS classes or CSS variables.
- Use CSS variables for theming.
- Never use `!important`.

### Mobile
- Use `StyleSheet.create` for styles.
- Define `StyleSheet.create` declarations before component props and component definitions.
- Do not use CSS modules or CSS custom properties.
